[gd_scene format=3 uid="uid://unit_standard_material_default_fade_lit"]

; What it holds: four meshes that draw Godot's default material, on a ground with no material: a sphere whose material file
; cannot load, a box with no material, and two spheres that fade, one by GeometryInstance3D transparency and one by visibility
; range with fade mode self. A shadowed sun and a colour ambient light light them. They draw through Godot's generated shader and
; the lit scene template (?litSurface=nodes). Every other material golden draws the classic path, so only this one shows a
; regression in these surfaces on the node path.

